INT. SEASIDE BOARDING HOUSE - ATTIC - NIGHT

Slanted beams. A cracked skylight. Moonlight on trunks, hatboxes, a headless dressmaker's dummy. The air smells of salt and mildew.

Five guests have climbed the narrow stair with lanterns.

MRS. ODELIA PRINGLE (60s, shawl, a ring of keys) leads. DR. HORACE BLACKWOOD-ADE (50s, black bag, bowler hat) follows. Then MISS CONSTANCE TAMBLYN (20s, nightgown under a coat), clutching a candle. Behind her, MR. FERDINAND OKORO-STRAND (40s, braces, a revolver he clearly does not know how to hold), and last, young THOMAS (12, nightshirt, wide-eyed, a tin whistle).

ODELIA
(to the group)
Stay close. The floor is rotten in places.

HORACE
Mrs. Pringle, what precisely are we looking for?

ODELIA
The thing that has been tapping.

CONSTANCE
(whispering)
It tapped again last night.

FERDINAND
(to himself)
Nerves. Nothing but nerves.

THOMAS
It's not nerves.

ODELIA
Quiet, boy.

A single tap from behind the dummy. Everyone freezes. Constance's candle trembles. Ferdinand raises the revolver, then lowers it, then raises it again.

A second tap. A third. A scrape, as of fingernails on wood.

HORACE
(low)
Who is there?

The dummy topples. Dust billows. A dark shape lunges across the trunks. Constance screams. Ferdinand fires wildly, the shot punching a hole in the skylight. Horace dives behind a hatbox. Odelia swings her lantern. Thomas blows a shrill note on his whistle.

The shape hisses, springs up through the broken glass, and disappears into the night.

Silence. Glass tinkles. Moonlight pours through the new hole. The five of them stand panting among the trunks, one by one lowering their lanterns.

THOMAS
(softly)
It was a gull.

FERDINAND
(shakily)
A gull.

HORACE
A very large gull.

Odelia lifts the dummy upright with one hand and straightens its collar.

ODELIA
Back to bed, all of you.

She turns. One by one they file down the stairs. Thomas is last. He pauses at the top, tin whistle in hand, and looks back at the skylight.

Something taps. Once.
